From e66b1dca298523c84a8a7a0d9ae009ddf6562b10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:49:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: let the Sea of Runes reverse flow reach outlying grids

borg_flow_glyph() maps the distance from the borg to every candidate
rune grid with a reverse flow, then skips grids that are unreachable or
75 or more steps away.  It asked for an optimized spread, but the
reverse flow starts at the borg's own grid with cost 0, and an optimized
spread stops as soon as the next cost (1) exceeds the origin's cost.  No
other grid was ever given a cost, so the only candidate the scan could
see was the borg's own grid.

Once the centre rune is laid and the borg stands on it, that grid is
excluded from the outlying-rune choice, so the borg found nothing to do
and the Sea of Runes made no further progress while it stood there.

Spread the reverse flow without optimization, as the helper's own
comment ('do NOT optimize') intends.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#345.

(cherry picked from commit f618381294dcf5bff1f0bc95f0fbe259412a53b9)
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
index 5af26cf95..24872cc07 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
@@ -144,8 +144,9 @@ bool borg_flow_glyph(void)
         return false;
     }
 
-    /* Reverse flow */
-    borg_flow_reverse(250, true, false, false, -1, false);
+    /* Reverse flow, not optimized: it starts at the borg's own grid (cost 0)
+     * and an optimized spread stops before reaching any other grid. */
+    borg_flow_reverse(250, false, false, false, -1, false);
 
     /* Scan the entire map */
     for (y = 15; y < AUTO_MAX_Y - 15; y++) {
